Instead of using `str(value)`, use `json.dumps(value)` for non-string, non-numeric, non-boolean types. This will produce a standardized, more widely parsable representation for complex types like lists and dictionaries. You may need to import the `json` module.

```python
import json

# ... inside _propagate_attributes

